{
  "id": "Compound::DB00331 - Gene::4712",
  "verbalization": "Metformin is shown to interact with Ndufb6 through a series of mechanistic pathways that involve the Nadh Dehydrogenase (ubiquinone) and Nadh Dehydrogenase (quinone) activities. The evidence suggests that Metformin binds to Ndufa12 and Ndufv3, which are subunits of the Nadh Dehydrogenase complex, and that these subunits participate in the activity of Ndufb6. This indicates a potential role for Metformin in modulating the activity of Ndufb6, possibly through the inhibition of the Nadh Dehydrogenase complex. The consistent scores across the three paths suggest a robust and reliable relationship, supported by the shared involvement of Ndufb6 in the activity of the Nadh Dehydrogenase complex. The mechanism appears to involve the regulation of the Nadh Dehydrogenase complex, which is critical for cellular respiration and energy production. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential mechanism by which Metformin may influence Ndufb6, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm the exact nature of this interaction.",
